WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.220
I mentioned at the top of the show in our
first segment, sort of taking a big picture

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:10.180
look at what's going on and the options, the
two possible paths forward that the country

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.499
is facing right now in the wake of the riotous
insurrection from last week.

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:17.000
I talked about what's happening within the
Republican Party.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.470
And you have some Republicans that are bailing
on Donald Trump and you have some that are

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:22.470
not.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:27.510
And I made the point that the people that
are bailing with 11 days to go, this is not

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.620
an act of courage.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.170
This is an act of self-preservation.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:35.070
And it's really important that we not allow
these people to rehabilitate their reputations

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:41.190
because they've been part of it for a very
long time and only now when it is relatively

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.780
safe politically to do so.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.600
They are saying this is too much, that's too
much, too much.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.770
I can't be a part of it.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.660
But that being said, there is a growing list
of Republicans that now want to remove Donald

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.660
Trump.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.710
And I think it's important to understand that
this is different.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.489
We did not see this during the first impeachment,
as it looks like we are heading towards a

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:02.950
second impeachment of the president.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.620
So let's talk about it a little bit and go
through some of the instances.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.829
Republican Senator Lisa Murkowski, a sitting
senator, Republican from the state of Alaska,

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:17.469
says that she wants Trump out and may even
leave the Republican Party altogether over

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:18.469
this.

00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:21.009
Now, if she does leave, she's not saying she
would become a Democrat.

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:24.409
There's every indication that if she were
to leave the Republican Party, she would be

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:25.709
an independent.

00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:30.829
But she put out a statement pointing out that
Donald Trump incited this mob to unlawfully

00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:37.579
breach the Capitol, led to injured and in
fact, law enforcement deaths, put members

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:42.100
of Congress in danger, put the vice president
in danger, interfered with the duty of Congress

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.079
to count the electoral votes.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:47.539
And she goes on to say that Donald Trump indeed
should leave.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:49.349
Lisa Murkowski saying, I think he should leave.

00:01:49.349 --> 00:01:51.399
He said he's not going to show up.

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:53.189
He's not going to appear at the inauguration.

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:55.670
He hasn't been focused on what's going on
with covid.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:59.490
He's either been golfing or he's been inside
the Oval Office fuming and throwing every

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:03.990
person who's been loyal and faithful to him
under the bus, starting with the vice president.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.840
He only wants to stay there for the title.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.259
She says he only wants to stay there for his
ego.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:10.390
He needs to get out.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.739
He needs to do the good thing.

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:13.900
But I don't think he's capable of doing a
good thing.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.790
So an important statement from Republican
Lisa Murkowski.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.849
She's not saying she would vote to convict.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:21.790
She's saying Trump should leave, Trump should
resign.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:26.349
And it's not clear that there's even a one
percent chance that he does that.

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:33.790
And, yes, she also went on to say that the
her future may not be in the Republican Party,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.730
but it's not in the Democratic Party either.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.500
Every indication is Lisa Murkowski would become
an independent if she were to leave the party.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.200
But it's something it's still a big deal.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.590
Another current Republican Senator, Pat Toomey,
says remove Trump.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.349
He's actually saying it is time to remove
Donald Trump.

00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:54.390
Take a listen to what he had to say yesterday
on one of the Sunday shows.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:58.630
Your Republican colleague, Senator Lisa Murkowski
of Alaska, says President Trump should resign.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.240
She said, quote, He's caused enough damage.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.459
Do you agree?

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:11.300
Yeah, I do I think at this point, with just
a few days left, it's the best path forward,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:18.010
the best way to get this person in the rearview
mirror for us, that could happen immediately.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.030
I'm not optimistic it will, but I do think
that would be the best way forward.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:25.630
So that is a big deal that that that that
is huge.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.030
There's no way around that.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.030
Yes.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.030
We're down to nine days left.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:33.420
But that is still you know, it's starting
to point to what we had.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:39.620
You know, when Richard Nixon was about to
be impeached, Republicans got together and

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.920
they went to him and they said, this is it,
this is it.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.859
You're getting impeached and we're going to
convict.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.510
And at that time, circumstances were very
different.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.689
And it's it's almost cliche and overly simplistic
to say Republicans then were willing to do

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:56.950
what Republicans today aren't willing to do.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.819
The Republican Party is also dramatically
more radical today than it was.

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:06.879
I think that today's Republican Party also
wouldn't have said to Nixon, it's time to

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.909
go, unfortunately.

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:12.530
But that was when there was something that
was beyond the line today.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.959
Nothing seems to be beyond the line for most
Republicans.

00:04:14.959 --> 00:04:16.900
So good for Pat Toomey.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.200
However, he then says in the same interview
that that voting for Trump made sense at the

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.200
time.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.910
After Wednesday's attack, he took to the Senate
floor to denounce President Trump as a demagog.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.630
But we should note, you voted for him in November
for the second time, even after Charlottesville.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.630
Right.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.100
Even after he used force to clear Lafayette
Square for a photo op, even after he embraced

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.950
Kuhnen conspiracy theorists, many of whom
were in that mob.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:43.220
I'm not saying you bear any responsibility
for what happened on Wednesday, but do you

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:49.540
regret not doing more to stop somebody you're
now now calling a demagog, who's pretty obviously

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.610
been a demagog for his entire political career?

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:57.250
It Jake, I don't think there's any doubt at
all, is not in my mind that the president's

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:02.140
behavior after the election was wildly different
than his behavior before he descended into

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:09.200
a level of madness and engaged in activity
that was just absolutely unthinkable and unforgivable.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.750
For four years, he often put out offensive
and objectionable tweets, actually, sometimes

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:14.900
dozens a day.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.880
I never felt and I still don't think that
my job was to be his the editor of his Twitter

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.850
feed, although I was very often critical.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.580
So you can see the direction that that's that's
going, right.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.710
I mean, these are pathetic defenses.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:33.930
If we all knew what the direction of Trump's
presidency was going to be, why couldn't they

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:34.930
know?

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:39.060
We knew in 2016 when Trump was elected that
this was going to become an authoritarian

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.060
nightmare.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.900
And Pat Toomey says, well, you know, other
than the mean tweets, it all seemed perfectly

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.090
reasonable at the time.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.090
No.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.120
And this is why I'm saying a lot of these
guys are doing this just out of self preservation.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:55.960
And then lastly, longtime Trump loyalist Chris
Christie says if inciting to insurrection

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:00.020
isn't impeachment worthy, then I really don't
know what is now.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.280
But if an impeachment resolution actually
comes to the floor, won't many Republicans

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.120
be hard pressed to oppose it?

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:11.990
Listen, I think they're all going to have
to vote their conscience and and look at what

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:17.900
happened, I mean, what we had was an incitement
to riot at the United States Capitol.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.220
We have people killed.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.950
And to me, there's not a whole lot of question
here.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.950
So, you know.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:27.010
So you think it was an impeachable offense
for George?

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:34.830
Oh, sure, yeah, and you'd vote to make, you
know, in the will, that's if I think it's

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:35.830
an impeachable offense.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.570
That's exactly what I would do, George, but
I'm not in there.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:39.570
But you want my opinion.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:40.570
That's my opinion.

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.570
I don't.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:45.610
I think if if inciting to insurrection isn't
that I don't really know what it is.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.860
But I will say, too, that the Democrats, by
what they did earlier on Ukraine, have kind

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.840
of cheapened this a little bit, too.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.040
So, you know, there's always a hedge.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:07:01.580
And Chris Christie says Democrats cheapened
impeachment with Ukraine, but, yeah, he should

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.530
be impeached this time.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.410
That's a big time Trump loyalist.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.550
That's a powerful Republican figure.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:14.400
That's a guy who was metaphorically and literally
behind Donald Trump for years, standing on

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.470
stage, sometimes looking a little sick from
the things Trump was saying.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:22.350
But it's a big deal that Chris Christie now
says, yes, this is absolutely impeachable.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:26.720
So there's no sympathy for any of these Republican
operatives.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.310
They were behind Trump for years.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:34.950
But it is important that it's also Republicans
this time to not because we need to allow

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:41.870
their image to be rehabilitated, but because
it confirms to us how bad things are that

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:46.930
even with the most radical Republican Party
we've arguably ever had, we are starting to

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:48.860
see some Republicans say it's time to go.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.860
Yeah, it's pathetic.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.160
It's only nine days to go.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.160
I get it.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:57.150
They don't get anything other than this does
signal how insane the situation has gotten.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:02.910
But one guy who I guess is going down with
the ship is Republican Senator Lindsey Graham.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:09:27.640
And I want to talk about him next.

